 ## Overview
-Sphere Carving is a voxel operation that removes solid voxels within a spherical radius from a center point in a chunk, primarily used for destructible terrain scenarios [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [3D Binary Sphere Kernel Generation](4654-3d-binary-sphere-kernel-generation.md), which generates a static binary mask, by actively modifying the voxel grid state (setting voxels to 0/air) and returning metadata about the destruction [S1, S3, unofficial]. It also differs from [Voxel Deformation with Spherical Falloff](4413-voxel-deformation-with-spherical-falloff.md), which uses continuous soft falloff for reversible editing, by performing hard-edged binary removal [S1, unofficial][S2].
+Sphere Carving is a voxel operation that removes solid voxels within a spherical radius from a center point in a chunk, primarily used for destructible terrain scenarios [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [3D Binary Sphere Kernel Generation](4654-3d-binary-sphere-kernel-generation.md), which generates a static binary mask, by actively modifying the voxel grid state (setting voxels to 0/air) and returning metadata about the destruction [S1, S3, unofficial]. It also differs from [Voxel Deformation with Spherical Falloff](4413-voxel-deformation-with-spherical-falloff.md), which uses continuous soft falloff for reversible editing, by performing hard-edged binary removal [S1, unofficial].
 
