 ### [Voxel Edit Brush Operations](6271-voxel-edit-brush-operations.md)
-Voxel Edit Brush Operations provide a set of interactive tools (Place, Carve, Fill, Paint) for modifying unbounded 3D voxel grids using world-space spherical or cylindrical selection volumes. The method solves the problem of real-time, view-independent sculpting and material insertion in volumetric data, ensuring consistent behavior across chunk boundaries by addressing voxels via unbounded world-grid coordinates rather than local indices. Unlike parent methods that may rely on sparse structures or offline processing, this approach often utilizes dense 3D textures for mask lookups to enable O(1) per-fragment operations, avoiding the performance penalty of per-fragment analytic SDF evaluations.
